      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "DESPICABLE ANDY (1) is a capable type and proved too strong last time to win by 0.8 lengths at Ballarat in a handy 25.70 beating Aston Mali. Yet to win out of this box but has been in the placings three times from four starts. Great chance again. MIKADO MANIA (2) was well back early but attacked the line strongly to finish third (30.11) at Sandown in Grade 4/5. Has been out the placings in all four runs here. Form from her last run is proving to be solid. Bold showing expected. PAW GELDOFF (4) has been out of the placings the last couple but was a Bottom Up - Grade 5 winner (25.90) three back at Warrnambool. Well placed here and should do much better. YOUNG RUFUS (3) should be thereabouts despite an unplaced run here most recently.",
